const compile = jest.spyOn(validator, 'compile');
jest.unstable_mockModule('ajv', () => ({
  Ajv: jest.fn(() => validator),
}));

const {ToolRegistry} = await import('./registry.js');

describe('ToolRegistry static compilation', () => {
  it('compiles a static schema once through the Ajv package entry point across ten calls (spec: specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#7)', async () => {
    const registry = new ToolRegistry();
    const inputs: Record<string, unknown>[] = [];
    const input = {location: 'Berlin', extra: 42};
    registry.register(
      {
        name: 'weather',
        description: 'Weather by location',
        inputSchema: {type: 'object', properties: {location: {type: 'string'}}, required: ['location']},
      },
      async received => {
        inputs.push(received);
        return 'sunny';
      }
    );
    const registrationCompiles = compile.mock.calls.length;

    for (let call = 0; call < 10; call++) {
      await registry.execute('weather', input);
    }

    expect({registrationCompiles, totalCompiles: compile.mock.calls.length, inputs}).toEqual({
      registrationCompiles: 1,
      totalCompiles: 1,
      inputs: Array.from({length: 10}, () => input),
    });
  });
});
# Tool Input Validation

| Field  | Value                |
| ------ | -------------------- |
| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
| Status | In Progress          |

Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.

## Validation at execute time

- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16), [validated by: rejects missing location before executing weather (spec: specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#2)](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.required.test.ts#L4)).
- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults.
- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake.

## Schema compilation and caching

- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94), [validated by: rejects a numeric required constraint for weather (spec: specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#6)](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L4)).
- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: compiles a static schema once through the Ajv package entry point across ten calls (spec: specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#7)](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.compilation.test.ts#L13)).
- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules ([validated by: validates weather against the current location schema (spec: specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#8)](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.dynamic.test.ts#L4)).

## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery

- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).

## Enum rejection diagnostics

- An input outside a declared enum is rejected before execution with a result naming the field path and the enum constraint, without echoing the supplied value ([validated by: rejects an unlisted weather unit with an enum diagnostic (spec: specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#10)](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.enum.test.ts#L4)).

## Rejection logging

- A rejected tool input emits a warning naming the tool, failing field path and constraint using the same diagnostic returned to the model, without recording supplied property values ([validated by: logs a nested location type rejection without its value (spec: specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#11)](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.diagnostics.test.ts#L5)).

