# Changelog

All notable changes to `@re-cinq/hal-engine` are documented here.

The format is [Keep a Changelog 1.1.0](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/), and this project adheres to
[Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html). Entries are written for somebody installing the
package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.

## [Unreleased]

### Changed

- Tool validation loads Ajv through its package entry point so the registry does not require consumers to resolve a dependency subpath.

- Invalid tool input now receives rejection text naming the failing JSON Schema constraint and field path, without including the supplied value. Rejections also emit a warning with the same diagnostic so operators can identify malformed calls without logging their payloads.

- Registering a static tool now compiles its JSON Schema immediately and rejects invalid schemas with an error naming the tool. Fix invalid schemas before starting the engine; static tools also return schema failures as tool results before their executors run. Function-valued definitions validate against the schema resolved for each call and reuse validators for previously seen schema objects. Executors receive only schema-valid input, so executors that previously handled malformed input themselves no longer receive those calls.

## [0.3.0] - 2026-09-17

### Changed

- `HalEngineConfig.orchestrator.hooks` now carries a JSDoc comment. The field already shipped
  in `0.2.x`; the comment makes the lifecycle-hook seam discoverable from the published type
  declarations so editors surface it on hover without a trip to the README.

